## Operation: PreviewRecipients

### Summary

The backend works out the customers a quick send's recipient reaches, and the staff member looks at them.

### Input

```schema
provider: string required
params: string required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationStaff`
- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The provider gives the ids of the customers of the staff member's organisation the parameters reach, each e-mail address once — [invokes](aim:juicebar.communications#Capability:RecipientProviders), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.send#Requirements[PREVIEW])
- The preview dialog shows those customers page by page — [invokes](aim:juicebar.communications#Capability:CustomerDirectory), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.send#Requirements[PREVIEW])
- The operation, and reading a provider's selection types, are refused without `communication:role` with its `send` permission — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES])

### Returns

- The customers' ids.

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/send/quick-send-panel/quick-send-panel.component.ts#QuickSendPanelComponent.prerender` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/send/preview-customers-dialog/preview-customers-dialog.component.ts#PreviewCustomersDialogComponent` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#prerenderRecipients` — as: handler
- binds: `service:entities#fetchEntities` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: QuickSend

### Summary

A staff member sends a message at once to a quick send's recipient.

### Input

```schema
channel: string required
recipient: part(juicebar.communications#Recipient) required
subject: string required
template: string required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationStaff`
- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The message runs at once as an active communication of the staff member's organisation, started by them, and is kept only in the history — [invokes](aim:juicebar.communications#Operation:RunCommunication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.send#Requirements[SENDDONE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[RUN])
- A send without a channel or without recipients is refused — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.send#Requirements[SENDCHANNEL])
- The staff member follows the run's progress, which the backend gives to any signed-in staff member — [reads](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:TaskQueue), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.send#Requirements[SENDDONE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[SESSIONONLY])
- The operation is refused without `communication:role`; its `send` permission is not asked — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES])

### Returns

- The id of the task that carries out the run.

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/send/quick-send-panel/quick-send-panel.component.ts#QuickSendPanelComponent.send` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#send` — as: handler
- binds: `service:communication-service#getQueue` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred
